n pulley/sprocket as found good condition.</p><p>&nbsp;4. Check lock hub and re-tightening.</p><p>&nbsp;5. Check belt tensioning and belt alignment.</p><p>&nbsp;6. Check protection guard condition and cleaned.</p><p>&nbsp;7. Re-tighten bolts and check cooler fan shaft &amp; bearing top and bottom.</p><p>&nbsp;8. Re-greasing cooler fan shaft bearing top and bottom.</p><p>&nbsp;9. Inspected cooler fan blades for crack &amp; damage as found good condition.</p><p>&nbsp;10. Check blades clearance between blade edge and casing.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; North = 20.00 mm. South = 16.00 mm. East = 16.00 mm. West = 20.00 mm.</p><p>&nbsp;11. Measure blades angle. All blades = 11 degree</p><p>&nbsp;12. Check condition of fan hub and hub tube and re-tightening.</p><p>&nbsp;13. Inspect and cleaning of air seal plate and mounting.</p><p>&nbsp;14. Clean all fan blades.</p><p>&nbsp;15. Check bearing top and bottom vibration sensor as found good condition.</p><p>&nbsp;16. Test run and data recording:&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;- Running hour = 62,021 Hrs.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;- Running current = 42.00 Amps.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;- VT-2445 = 0.19 mm/s</p><p>&nbsp;17. Cleaned up area skid unit.</p><div><br></div><div><br></div>', NULL, '2025-02-01 11:44:03', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, 'PTTEP\\AthiwatK', NULL, false, 'ART') RETURNING id INTO new_report_id;
